= Stress Test Findings — vsf-rsi v0.2.6 =

date: 2026-09-01
scope: adversarial challenge + 7-dimension stress test
method: 32 tests across noise, dimensionality, genome expressiveness, population, non-separable, adversarial attacks, scalability

== BREAKING POINTS DISCOVERED ==

=== BP-1: Genome Expressiveness (CRITICAL) ===
dimension: genome_expressiveness
problem: unit circle (x²+y² < 1)
result: 16.7% accuracy — worse than random (50%)
root_cause: genome only has threshold plus branch_count. The bridge genome_to_predicate maps to value > threshold — a 1D threshold cannot represent a 2D circular boundary.
impact: ANY problem requiring non-linear, multi-dimensional decision boundaries fails.
fix_required: genome must encode tree structure (nested conditions, boolean operators, feature selection)

=== BP-2: Non-Separable Problems (CRITICAL) ===
dimension: non_separable
problem: checkerboard XOR (x>0 XOR y>0)
result: 50% accuracy — equal to random
root_cause: no single threshold on any feature can separate the XOR pattern. The genome has no way to combine multiple features.
impact: any problem where the decision boundary is not axis-aligned fails.
fix_required: genome must support multi-feature combinations (AND, OR, NOT)

== AREAS OF ROBUSTNESS ==

=== ROB-1: Noise Tolerance ===
tested: SNR from 1.0 down to 0.01
result: 100% accuracy at all levels
note: the GA finds the optimal threshold even when signal is 1% of noise
limitation: this works because the ground truth IS a threshold on SNR

=== ROB-2: Dimensionality (XOR) ===
tested: 3D to 30D
result: 83-100% accuracy across all dimensions
note: genome_to_predicate hardcodes XOR computation for the xor scenario type
limitation: this is a bridge artifact, not genome capability

=== ROB-3: Population Pressure ===
tested: populations of 2 to 20
result: 100% accuracy even with population=2
note: elite preservation plus small population still finds optimum
limitation: diversity loss is total (all thresholds converge), but it converges to the right answer

=== ROB-4: Adversarial Attacks ===
tested: bimodal, label flipping, distribution shift
result: bimodal=100%, label flip=83.3%, distribution shift=100%
note: label flipping at boundary causes 17% accuracy drop
limitation: the GA can be confused by adversarial label noise at the decision boundary

=== ROB-5: Scalability ===
tested: 20 to 500 scenarios
result: 100% accuracy, less than 1s for all sizes
note: linear scaling, no performance issues

== IMPROVEMENT CANDIDATES ==

1. GENOME-V2: richer genome representation
   - tree structure (nested if/else)
   - boolean operators (AND, OR, NOT)
   - feature selection (which context fields to use)
   - multi-threshold (multiple decision boundaries)
   priority: CRITICAL — without this, RSI can only solve threshold problems

2. BRIDGE-REDESIGN: genome_to_predicate must be generic
   - current: hardcoded per scenario type
   - needed: genome encodes the full predicate logic
   priority: HIGH — current bridge is a cheat code

3. FITNESS-FUNCTION: adversarial fitness must be scenario-agnostic
   - current: uses scenario_type to select evaluation logic
   - needed: genome encodes how to evaluate, fitness measures accuracy
   priority: HIGH — current fitness function knows too much

4. CONVERGENCE-DETECTION: track diversity loss
   - current: diversity_loss detected but not acted on
   - needed: inject random genomes when diversity drops
   priority: MEDIUM — would help with small populations

5. MULTI-OBJECTIVE: fitness should balance accuracy plus complexity plus generalization
   - current: accuracy-only fitness
   - needed: Pareto frontier across multiple objectives
   priority: MEDIUM — would reduce overfitting risk

== KEY INSIGHT ==

The GA is a competent optimizer — it finds the best threshold reliably.
The bottleneck is NOT the optimization algorithm.
The bottleneck is the GENOME REPRESENTATION.

Current genome: threshold plus branch_count — can only solve 1D threshold problems.
Needed genome: tree_structure plus operators plus features — can solve arbitrary boolean logic.

This is the fundamental limitation: RSI can optimize parameters, but it cannot
discover new strategies. The genome is a parameter tuner, not a strategy learner.

